        "action" : "weighing you against a jar of summer sunshine",
        "object" : "a brass pair of shop scales",
        "notes" : "“Shall I compare thee to a summer's day?” Under the Woolworth Building, Frank W. Woolworth, king of the five-and-dime, sets you on one pan of his brass shop scales and a jar of bottled summer sunshine on the other, and asks whether he should compare you."
      }
